        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile, possibly garment piece, phulkari, red cotton, embroidered, Hazara, ca. 1855-1879"@en , "Length of terracotta-coloured cotton, joined together, possibly a garment, embroidered with floss silk, the field is embroidered with an all over design resembling grain, wide diagonal bands of gold-coloured embroidery in the hems, narrow gold coloured design in the borders. Complete piece."@en , "Possibly intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en ;
